nodes.body:
@root1iu I don't see a use-case where a connector would send and recv concurrently.
A request first loads its KVs, then starts forward passes which can lead to KV sending.
This specific crash is due to a connector (LMCacheMP) which returns True on request_finished for a request that never actually finished loading. That makes no sense to me.

